# The newest upstream/develop commit that qariah-main contains (TECH_DEBT #236).
#
# scripts/lint-qariah-owned.mjs reads this SHA. A file that exists in the upstream
# tree at this commit is an upstream file, and the blocking ESLint step skips
# it. Every other tracked .js, .ts or .tsx file is Qariah-owned.
#
# Each upstream absorption PR updates this line. The weekly sync workflow
# (.github/workflows/upstream-sync.yml) does it in the same PR, in a second commit.
# For a merge that you make by hand, run this after the merge:
#   git fetch upstream develop
#   node scripts/lint-qariah-owned.mjs --update-pin
# The command writes `git merge-base HEAD upstream/develop` below. Keep the
# comment lines. The first line that is not a comment is the SHA, in full
# (40 characters).
